linuxmuster-common (1:7.4.5~edu) lmn74; urgency=low

  * edulution fork. The package keeps its upstream name, so the epoch 1: is
    what makes it win against the same package from deb.linuxmuster.net.
    A missing epoch counts as 0, so every existing versioned dependency on
    linuxmuster-common stays satisfied.
  * The version carries the suffix ~edu on top of the epoch, so apt policy,
    dpkg -l and the motd show at a glance that this is the edulution build
    and not the upstream package. "~" sorts before the empty string, so
    1:7.4.5~edu stays below a hypothetical 1:7.4.5 while still outranking
    every upstream 7.x, which carries no epoch at all.
  * Release workflow publishes to edulution-io/edulution-package-server
    instead of linuxmuster/deb, into the Ubuntu codename resolute.
  * Depend on edulution-archive-keyring, which owns
    /usr/share/keyrings/edulution.gpg, the keyring the sources entry for
    package.edulution.io names. New or rotated signing keys then reach the
    host with a regular upgrade.

 -- Lukas Lukic-Spitznagel <lukas.spitznagel@netzint.de>  Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

linuxmuster-common (7.4.5) lmn74; urgency=low

  * keep python bytecode caches out of the package: clean lib/__pycache__ in
    debian/rules and exclude __pycache__/*.pyc from dh_install, which
    "debian/install" pulled in via "lib/*".
  * postinst: byte-compile environment.py on "configure" instead of on
    "abort-upgrade|abort-remove|abort-deconfigure", where it never ran on a
    normal installation.

